d  childish  and not actually uh serious in any way  that gen saki and even joe biden  seem to enjoy taking questions from  peter like if it were actually the case  that this guy was asking such tough  questions and putting them in such  difficult positions  they wouldn't be so eager to hear from  him they almost seem entertained  by it and uh it's almost a curiosity to  see what flaccid nonsense  peter ducey's going to come up with next  and you get the feeling that gen saki  treats peter ducey and in some cases  that newsmax reporter named emerald who  was in the room  last week or the week before um she's  sort of treating them  like you treat one of your kids when  they're having a temper tantrum and she  has young kids  you humor it you allow them to say the  thing they want to say  and then you move on while showing that  it's not really something mommy is  impressed with and that's the  that's the vibe i get from jen saki  during these moments  now after this failed peter ducey tries  again  apparently with a quote real question it  doesn't really go much better  it's almost sometimes when he's reading  his questions like he's struggling to  understand because the emphasis and the  syntax  seems strange i don't really know let's  take a look  quickly on immigration the governor of  tennessee says that he was asked and he  declined a biden administration request  to  house unaccompanied minors and in coming  days  or in recent days there have been some  reports that at least four planes  filled with unaccompanied minders landed  in his state some in the middle of the  night  can you explain what's going on there  well as we have been very clear about  children our objective is to unite these  unaccompanied children  children under the age of 18 with  families with sponsor families so  children  traveling through we're traveling  through have been traveling through  tennessee  uh they're simply on their way to unite  with relatives and sponsors to meet  sponsor